    "teacherReflection": "After the lesson, check: Did learners use long division correctly and see that a repeating remainder gives repeating digits? Which misconception was most common: 'any decimal that goes on is irrational' (1/3 recurs, so it is rational) or 'π equals 22/7 or 3.14'? Did learners connect the rational family to Achieng's duka numbers (3, 1/2, 22.50 = 45/2)? Did cold-calling reach quiet learners, and was WAIT TIME of 10-15 seconds used? For the next lesson, prepare the square-field squaring checks (1.414 × 1.414 = 1.999396, 1.4142 × 1.4142 = 1.99996164, 1.415 × 1.415 = 2.002225) so learners can test why √2 never ends. Note which learners need more practice with long division and plan a short support group.",
