        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Look at the DQB. Which question can we now answer, and what is the evidence?' WAIT TIME: 10-15 seconds. Cold-call 3 learners to place a note and read it aloud. Ask: 'Which new question should we investigate next lesson?' Point out that the next lesson uses mathematical tables and the calculator 1/x key, and that Lesson 7 uses reciprocals in speed, time and savings. Remind the learners to take care of the DQB and keep notes neat (Responsibility).",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Driving Question Board with Gallery Walk: tracking questions publicly shows progress, helps learners see how each lesson answers a part of the Driving Question, and provides ownership of the next steps.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Observe whether learners place notes under the correct question numbers (6 and 7), whether notes contain evidence (numbers) and not just opinion, and whether at least 3 new, relevant questions are produced. Make a count of how many learners contribute a note."
