        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Add a reciprocal box to your model and connect it to the duka. Explain the connection in one sentence.' Circulate and ask: 'Where does the reciprocal sit in our map of real numbers?' WAIT TIME: 10-15 seconds. Cold-call 3 groups to show their models (Lake Victoria, Impala, Rift Valley). Ask one group to state the rule in 15 words. Close: 'Next lesson we will see how mathematical tables and the calculator 1/x key give reciprocals, and how accurate they are.' Collect the Summary Table as an exit ticket.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Model revision with a concept map: adding the new idea and drawing connecting arrows to the anchoring phenomenon forces learners to integrate reciprocal with number types and unit price, supporting a coherent story across the unit.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Check that each model includes: the definition 1/n = 1 ÷ n, the product n × 1/n = 1, at least 3 correct examples, the unit price link (90 × 1/6 = 15), and the zero exception. Exit ticket: 'Write the reciprocal of 8 and prove it.' (0.125 and 8 × 0.125 = 1.) Record how many learners get it right."
